# Swift Conventions

Source of truth: `iOSApp/AGENT.md` §6–§7, §11–§13.

## Async / concurrency

- **Hard ban:** never `.onAppear { Task { await … } }` — SwiftUI does not cancel that `Task`; `onAppear` can also fire more than once
- **Load / refresh bound to a view:** use `.task { await … }` (auto-cancels on disappear)
- **Reload when an identity changes** (or when a root list should refresh after pop): `.task(id:) { await … }` — cancels the previous task and starts a new one
- `.onAppear` is OK only for **sync** UI (start animation, set focus) — never spawn unstructured `Task`s there
- Button / gesture handlers may use `Task { await … }` (user-driven, not view-lifecycle)
- Independent work → `async let` or `TaskGroup`, not sequential `await`
- Stream tokens with `AsyncThrowingStream`; update `@Published` incrementally
- Use `defer { isLoading = false }` so loading always clears
- Check `Task.checkCancellation()` in long loops
- All ViewModels: `@MainActor`. Heavy CPU: `Task.detached` — never `DispatchQueue.main.async`

```swift
// ❌ BAD — unstructured Task; keeps running after disappear; can re-fire
.onAppear { Task { await viewModel.loadData() } }

// ✅ GOOD — cancelled when the view disappears
.task { await viewModel.loadData() }

// ✅ GOOD — also re-runs when id changes (previous task cancelled)
.task(id: userID) { await viewModel.loadUser(userID) }
.task(id: router.path.count) {
    guard router.path.isEmpty else { return }
    await viewModel.loadSessions() // e.g. refresh list after pop
}
```

## Errors

- Map failures to typed `AppError` with user-facing `errorDescription` / `isRetryable`
- Catch `AppError` at the ViewModel boundary; never show raw `Error.localizedDescription`
- LLM: rate-limit/quota on primary → one fallback retry → then `AppError.llmCallFailed`
- Prefer `do/catch` (or `guard` / `throws`) over force unwrap / `try!` / `as!`
- Log failures with `AppLogger` (`Core/Logging/AppLogger.swift`) — uses `NSLog` today; later forwards to Sentry
- Bootstrap that can fail (e.g. `DatabaseManager.shared`) returns optional / handled error UI — never `try!`

```swift
// ❌ BAD
static let shared = try! DatabaseManager()

// ✅ GOOD
static let shared: DatabaseManager? = {
    do {
        return try DatabaseManager()
    } catch {
        AppLogger.error("Failed to open or migrate memory.db", error: error)
        return nil
    }
}()
```

## Naming

| Thing | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Protocol | `*Protocol` | `MemoryRepositoryProtocol` |
| Use case | `VerbNounUseCase` | `SaveMemoryUseCase` |
| View / VM | `FeatureNameView(Model)` | `ChatViewModel` |
| Display model | `*DisplayModel` | `MessageDisplayModel` |
| Bools | `is`/`has`/`can`/`should` | `isLoading`, `canRetry` |
| Enum cases | lowerCamelCase | `.store`, `.query` |

## Style

- File order: imports → type → published → private props → init → public → private → extensions
- Size/complexity limits: see `ios-complexity.mdc` (functions ≤ 30, files/types ≤ 300, nesting ≤ 2, ≤ 4 params, ≤ 6 injected deps)
- Default to `private`; `@Published private(set)` for read-only UI state
- No force unwraps (`!`), `try!`, or `as!` — use `do/catch`, `guard let`, or `throws` + `AppLogger`

## Tests

- AAA pattern; name `test_method_expectedBehavior`
- Mock via protocols (`MockMemoryRepository`, etc.)
- Unit-test use cases, ViewModels, guards; integration-test repos with in-memory SQLite
- Views: Previews are enough — no logic in Views to test
